<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3536" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Arganthōnĭus</span></b> ,
		ii, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀργανθώνιος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a Tartessian king who lived to a great age</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Cic.
				Sen. 19, 69</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Val. Max. 8, 13</span></i>, ext. 4 (cf. Herod.
			1, 163); <i><span class="en">Plin. 7, 48, 49, § 154</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Censor. 17</span></i>.—Hence,
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Arganthōnĭăcus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>of</i>
			or <i>pertaining to Arganthonius</i>, <i><span class="en">Sil. 3,
			396</span></i>.</div>
